  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>z</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi></math></p><p>Also given,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>i</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>i</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>This is the equation of circle whose centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math>. Now, the line touches the circle</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
